   "source": [
    "data_df.plot(x=\"Primary_Platform\" ,y=\"Daily_Usage_Hours\", figsize=(12,6), linewidth=2,title= \"social_media_impact\",ylabel=\"Daily_Usage_Hours\",xlabel=\"Primary_Platform\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6c4d8756",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For the *line graph*, we had the social media platforms on the X-axis, then daily usage hours on the y-axis. \n",
    "\n",
    "## __EXPLANATION__\n",
    "The graph does *not* _accurately_ show the relationship between the platforms and the daily usage hours. \n",
    "\n",
    "## *What it shows:* \n",
    "• Few students use the platforms for few hours (2-3 hrs).\n",
    "\n",
    "• Most students use the platforms averagely (4-7 hrs). \n",
    "\n",
    "• A few use the platforms for so long (upto 14 hours a day.)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "017e779c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## __WHAT CONCLUSION CAN WE GET FROM THE DATASET?__\n",
    "    We conclude that spending a lot of time on *Social media* might lower our GPA or might increase it \n",
    "From the statistics and visualizations made we can see some people who spend a lot of time on social media perform badly while others perform even better than those who don't use it.\n",
    "-   The possibility for those who perform well is that they might be acquiring knowledge from social media and those who don't might be using it for non academic purposes."
   ]
  }
